cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this code, please cite the software below AND the dataset and the
  paper being replicated, both of which are listed under references.
title: "Age-regression bias in the AI ECG age gap: a replication on CODE-15%"
abstract: >-
  A replication, on the Brazilian CODE-15% cohort, of the finding that the
  AI-predicted ECG age gap is confounded by chronological age, and that
  correcting the confound reverses the direction of the crude survival result.
  A linear age-bias correction was applied by Hirota et al. (Japanese cohort,
  2023), and Barthels et al. (Belgian cohort, 2025) used it with mortality as
  the outcome; this repository repeats Barthels' method on CODE-15%. It adds an age- and sex-adjusted Cox comparison, a sex-fairness result
  for the pooled correction, and a null result for correcting within sex. Runs
  on the Python standard library with no third-party dependencies.
type: software
authors:
